good morning everyone or afternoon I  don't know where it what time is it  wherever you are here currently it is 5  32 in the morning and I am super excited  for today's video because this is very  special to me this channel has been  growing steadily and first of all I just  want to say thank you for your support  but I thought it would be a really fun  way to do like a q a get to know me kind  of video but also as a way to connect  with you and really get to know you so  if you have any kind of videos that you  would like to see and anything that kind  of pops up just put it down in the  comments and we can chat together so I'm  really excited about today especially  though because there's a lot of really  good questions and specifically on time  management I'm really excited to get  into that so without a further Ado let's  get on with today's video the first  question is one that I am actually asked  a lot and so I thought I'd take a fun  spin on it and ask you the question  instead and that is where do you think  that I am from go ahead put your guests  down in the comments I'm curious to know  what you think  did you do it yet okay well I currently  live here in the USA I am a U.S citizen  however I was born and raised in Mexico  when I was a child right smack in the  middle of nowhere  was that your guess up until I was seven  I lived in an area of poverty where most  people did not have running water AC or  Heating and really things like  microwaves and refrigerators were  unheard of I don't remember a whole lot  about my childhood but I am grateful  that I grew up poor because it really  helped shape me and it gave me a greater  gratitude for the lifestyle that I get  to have here in the USA and just the way  that I can also teach my children as  well but what about you where are you  watching from let me know down in the  comments below greetings from the USA  the next question is what do I do for a  living I think that some people might  think that this question may be dull or  superficial but for me it is a very  important question actually because I am  a home hospice nurse that means that I  work with patients that are end stages  of life and my entire job is to help  manage their symptoms so that they can  live their best life for as long as they  have while also giving the family the  resources they need to be able to take  care of their loved ones while this job  can certainly be difficult on an  emotional level I think that for me it  motivates me to live all the more  because of the fact that I am constantly  faced with patients that are dying it  really helps remind me that my life is  ever passing and that I should take  advantage of the time that I have and  really Savor each moment to be a better  wife to be a better mother to be a  better friend and just really value my  time so much more it really makes me  want to be present and Savor each day  next up human brother asks how do I  manage work and YouTube first of all  thank you so much for your support and  thank you for this question because I am  very passionate about work life balance  so I will try not to rant on this topic  because I am sure I could devote an  entire video to this topic so I will try  to keep it to the main three points so  by now you know that I'm a full-time  nurse but I also have a four-year-old a  one-year-old and as you can see I have  this YouTube channel as well so when it  comes to work-life balance I've  developed a few rules that really help  keep me sane so that I can be the best  version of me to those around me because  I work as a home nurse and I work off of  my personal phone having the ability  disconnect from my phone is crucially  important because I constantly get  threads of messages from co-workers or  even my boss asking if anybody wants to  work overtime and it may sound really  rude but I silence those and if I'm  doing something when I'm not working I  turn my phone off and I think that  having this rule for myself is immensely  important because it creates this  barrier like this is me time you don't  pass this threshold and if you don't  respect your time nobody else is going  to do it for you so find whatever  barriers that you need because it can be  really easy to let work creep home with  you if you let it so the first tip would  be is to separate work from home and  find however best that would work for  you secondly is that I wake up between 5  and 5 30 a.m almost every day I have a  full video on how to wake up at 5am  feeling glorious if you want to develop  a morning habit and wake up earlier I'll  leave it in the description below but  for me this is a must I was not always a  morning person it was not something that  I enjoyed but the more I did it the more  I found that for me it's like gold my  kids usually wake up at 7 30 so these  two-ish hours are crucial for me they  allow me to wake up without feeling  rushed to be able to have time to be  still to pray to work on a YouTube video  I'm filming right now and it's 5 32 in  the morning well actually it was 5 32  when I started but all those sorts of  things that I can do for myself it's  it's my me time and I value that so much  because really my most productive and  peaceful hours of my day happened before  the sun rises I don't think that I would  get anything done if I did not wake up  early and third is I have learned not to  push myself more than I should and just  to slow down I talk more about that in  my video on why I quit the fire movement  I think that just Society in general  really values busyness I mean you ask  somebody how they're doing and more  often than not they'll say I'm busy and  for a long time I thought that this was  a good thing I thought that it meant  that I was hard working that my life was  was interesting and through my work as a  nurse especially in hospice nursing and  as a mom in general I just have come to  Value Stillness and slow intentional  living so much more in Spanish there is  a saying  that means if you try to do many things  your ability to do those things well  will be reduced I now make a priority of  my family and my health and sadly it was  not always that way I was the type of  individual that would just push push  push to get to this goal even at the  expense of burnout and my health and  that's just not the life that I want  anymore and that's not the life that you  deserve either you deserve rest and I  think that it's important to work and  it's important to do meaningful things  but we often forget the rest portion so  finding a happy medium between being  able to do those things but at the same  time making time for that rest and  making time for fun is huge so really  take inventory of all the activities  that you have either on a daily or  weekly basis and find which ones are  those priorities that you absolutely  should get done done or want to get done  and just cut out the ones where you can  and make time for that rest time for me  unfortunately that means that I cannot  post videos every single week at the  moment hopefully someday we'll be able  to get there for now it is every two  weeks but it is a goal it eventually  will happen I thank you for your  patience in the meantime though I  apologize that I rancid on this question  but in this ever busy world we live in I  think it's such an important topic to  talk about this next question is what  are my favorite apps for task management  oh I'm glad you asked this question  hands down Google Calendar is my  favorite app for task managing because  in the past I used to write my little  to-do list and I'd have my things of  what I wanted to do for that day or for  that week and more often than not they  would just happen tomorrow tomorrow  tomorrow and push them down further why  because they were never scheduled and so  now I basically live by Google Calendar  and I schedule all sorts of to-do's like  if I have to go to the Post Office it's  scheduled at a specific time taking my  daughter to physical therapy okay that's  scheduled two all of those things I can  schedule on my calendar and be able to  see everything that I have to do and  then also not put too much on my plate  because I'm able to see all the things  that I have to do for that day so it  makes it more likely that I'm actually  going to be able to do them and it helps  me kind of prioritize what's more  important for which particular day also  I love the fact that I can color code  them so that it makes it much easier for  me to organize everything that I have to  do so for example my work days are in  red my YouTube videos and filming and  all those sorts of things are in green  any other kind of activities or if I'm  visiting someone I'll put them in a  different color it really just helps me  kind of visualize in a much more  organized way but also one of the things  that I really love about Google Calendar  is that you can share it because you  make an account you're able to share it  with individuals so if my husband wants  to edit something he has a dentist  appointment he can go in there and he  can edit it so hands down I love Google  Calendar and it's completely free and  then the next app that I use is really  just the notes app on my phone I used to  use Evernote especially for my recipes  if something would turn out good because  I would take a picture of my food and I  could put the picture and the  description on that but then it has a  paid for version and it was constantly  giving me the pop-ups asking me to  upgrade and I'm not all about that so I  just used the notes app on my phone  really for just any ideas that I get  especially like YouTube videos I have to  write them down because otherwise I will  forget so between these two things they  work out perfectly for me one is like an  agenda kind of organizing my day and  then the other is just I get a random  idea let's jot it down this last  question is a bit of a random one it is  do I have pets um actually no I used to  have a rabbit a long long time ago I  have chickens but those don't really  count I don't have any cats or dogs  actually I have a big fear of big dogs  my grandma was bit by a dog years ago  and I remember the wound vividly and  ever since then I've just always had  this major fear of big dogs and you  would think that as a home nurse after  the constant exposure I would have  gotten over this fear but only recently  it was about a month ago I was chased  down the street by one of my patients  dogs as I was about to enter the home  and let's just say that the anxiety  returned with a Vengeance and I really  wanted to quit my job that day my  co-workers make fun of me actually  because I'm always the person to type in  the notes they have a big dog make sure  make sure you know they have a big dog  my co-workers have told me that I should  probably just get a dog as a puppy and  that being a dog owner would help me and  I could see that I could actually  picture myself with a big fluffy dog  jogging down the street and I don't know  what else we would do probably cuddle it  would be fluffy that's one thing I know  it would be fluffy but first of all I  wouldn't even know what kind of a breed  to get so that's probably something that  would maybe maybe happen someday in the  future that's probably not going to get  scheduled on the Google Calendar  but what about you do you have any pets  and if you are a dog owner please I will  take all the tips that you can give me  on how to combat this it's rather silly  and embarrassing truthfully that is it  for today's video these are just a few  short questions but I hope I did not  rant too much and hopefully I provided  some value to you if you like this video  please give it a thumbs up and help  support my channel I thank you so so  much for your support and for taking  this time with me I can't wait to hear  from you in the comments and just learn  more from you and please let me know  what kind of suggestions you have for  future videos going forward I look  forward to hearing from you in the  comments and I'll see you in the next  video until next time bye for now

